# mw-vectors.golden --- MW (MEMORY CHANNEL WRITE), Set-direction frames
#
# SOURCE MANUAL
#   Title (cover, PDF page 1):  FT-891  CAT Operation Reference Book
#   Publisher:                  YAESU MUSEN CO., LTD.  (Copyright 2019)
#   Printed revision:           1909-C   (printed bottom-right of the back cover,
#                               PDF page 20; the cover carries no revision)
#   Chart used:                 MW command block, printed folio 13, PDF page 14
#   Command-list entry:         printed folio 3, PDF page 4
#   Derivation date:            04/09/2026
#
# METHOD
#   Located at 300 dpi; the MW block re-rendered at 600 dpi (pdftoppm -r 600) and
#   cropped in two overlapping strips with magick, because at 300 dpi the chart's
#   three numbered rows sit alongside the legend column and the position numbers
#   are not unambiguous. Two independent counts (left-to-right across rows
#   1-10 / 11-20 / 21-30, then by per-parameter cell totals) both gave 28; no
#   third look was needed.
#
#   NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# WHICH CHART THE LAYOUT WAS COUNTED FROM, AND WHY
#   Counted from the MW *Set* chart -- the only filled chart in the block. The MW
#   Read and Answer charts are printed but their value rows are BLANK, which
#   agrees with the command list (Read "X", Ans. "X"). There is therefore no
#   second filled MW chart to cross-check against; the count was instead
#   cross-checked against the MR *Answer* chart on printed folio 12, which prints
#   the same 28-position layout with the same parameter labels (M,R in place of
#   M,W). That is a cross-command check, not a within-block one -- noted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTH: 28 bytes (terminator included)
#
# POSITION-BY-POSITION FIELD MAP (MW Set chart, counted)
#   pos  1      "M"        command character (printed literal)
#   pos  2      "W"        command character (printed literal)
#   pos  3- 5   P1         legend verbatim: "P1  001 - 099 (Regular Memory Channel)"
#                                           "    P1L - P9U (PMS)"
#   pos  6-14   P2         legend verbatim: "P2  Frequency (Hz)"       (9 positions counted)
#   pos 15      "+/-"      printed literally as "+/-" in the chart cell; covered by
#                          the P3 legend line below
#   pos 16-19   P3         legend verbatim: "P3  Clarifier Direction +: Plus Shift, -: Minus Shift"
#                                           "    Clarifier Offset: 0000 - 9999 (Hz)"
#   pos 20      P4         legend verbatim: "P4  0: CLAR "OFF"    1: CLAR "ON""
#   pos 21      P5         legend verbatim: "P5  0: (Fixed)"
#   pos 22      P6         legend verbatim: "P6  MODE  1: LSB    2: USB    3: CW    4: FM    5: AM    6: RTTY-LSB    7: CW-R"
#                                           "          8: DATA-LSB    9: RTTY-USB    A: -    B: FM-N    C: DATA-USB"
#                                           "          D: AM-N"
#   pos 23      P7         legend verbatim: "P7  0: (Fixed)"
#   pos 24      P8         legend verbatim: "P8  0: CTCSS "OFF"    1: CTCSS ENC/DEC    2: CTCSS ENC"
#   pos 25-26   P9         legend verbatim: "P9  00: (Fixed)"        (2 positions counted)
#   pos 27      P10        legend verbatim: "P10 0: Simplex    1: Plus Shift    2: Minus Shift"
#   pos 28      ";"        terminator (printed literal)
#
#   There is NO tag parameter on this command: the MW chart stops at position 28
#   and the MW legend has no P11 or P12 entry.
#
# BYTES THE MANUAL DETERMINES
#   pos 1-2 (M,W), pos 21 (P5 fixed "0"), pos 23 (P7 fixed "0"), pos 25-26 (P9
#   fixed "00"), pos 28 (";"). Every other position's set of legal values is
#   printed; the particular value chosen below is mine from that set.
#
# INHERITED-ASSUMED BYTES
#   1. FREQUENCY RANGE (pos 6-14). The MW legend prints only "Frequency (Hz)" with
#      no range. Inherited the FA/FB range printed on printed folio 9 (PDF page
#      10), "P1  000030000 - 056000000 (Hz)", to keep the chosen values inside
#      what this manual permits. INHERITED-ASSUMED that the MW P2 range equals the
#      VFO range.
#   2. CLARIFIER CONSISTENCY (pos 15-20). Not printed whether pos 16-19 must read
#      "0000" when P4 is "0" (CLAR "OFF"), nor whether the pos-15 sign is
#      meaningful at zero offset. ASSUMED "+0000" with P4="0" for the
#      no-clarifier vectors.
#   3. PARAMETER-COMBINATION LEGALITY. The manual never says which combinations of
#      mode, shift and CTCSS a channel may hold. ASSUMED the combinations below
#      are accepted.
#   4. WHICH SLOT NAMES MW ACCEPTS. The MW P1 legend lists only "001 - 099
#      (Regular Memory Channel)" and "P1L - P9U (PMS)" -- not the "501 - 510
#      (5 MHz, U.S. and U.K. version only)" or "EMG (Emergency)" that the MR
#      block's P0/1 legend lists. No vector below uses those. Recorded, not
#      resolved.
#
# DIRECTION SUPPORT: the command list (printed folio 3, PDF page 4) prints
#   Command "MW" | Function "MEMORY WRITE" | Set "O" | Read "X" | Ans. "X" | AI "X",
#   and the MW detail block agrees: its Read and Answer value rows are blank.
#   (Only the block *title* differs -- see provenance.md.)
#
# HARDWARE STATUS: UNVERIFIED for every vector below.
#
# The three cases mirror MT cases 1, 5 and 6 (same channel, frequency, mode,
# clarifier, CTCSS and shift content; no tag on this command).

mw_ch001_7m100_lsb	MW001007100000+000000100000;
mw_pms_p1l_3m500_lsb	MWP1L003500000+000000100000;
mw_ch010_51m000_fm_clar_minus_ctcss_encdec_minus_shift	MW010051000000-025010401002;
